{"id":"wikibooks:hot-sauce-homemade","verdict":"keep","recipes":[{"source":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook%3AHot_Sauce_(Homemade)","status":"fixed","reason":"Decode HTML dash entity.","ingredients":["1–5 cloves of garlic, depending on size and taste","Vinegar (any kind)","Lime juice","1–3 squirts of honey","About 10 habanero peppers, de-stemmed","Salt"],"steps":["Mix all ingredients except peppers and honey in blender until you think you've got enough liquid. It doesn't matter how much of anything you use—just throw it all in. As a general rule, though, your total liquid volume should be about the size of 3–4 peppers. Make sure it covers up to the middle of the blender blades.","Pulse everything until smooth.","Add habaneros and pulse more, until they're fairly chopped up but still chunky.","Add honey, and blend for about 30 seconds. Your resulting sauce should be fairly thick, but contain only very small particles of peppers and garlic. If there are chunks bigger than grains of salt, keep blending until they are tiny."]}]}
{"id":"wikibooks:hot-water-crust-pastry","verdict":"keep","recipes":[{"source":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook%3AHot_Water_Crust_Pastry","status":"fixed","reason":"Two alternative dough methods were concatenated; retain method one.","ingredients":["170 g (6 oz) flour","170 ml (6 fl oz) water","85 g (3 oz) lard","1 pinch salt"],"steps":["Sift the flour and salt into a bowl. Make a well in the centre.","Place the water and lard into a saucepan over low heat. When the lard has melted, bring to a boil.","Pour the mixture into the centre of the flour.","Working very quickly, mix with a wooden spoon.","Knead briefly with hands to produce a smooth dough."]}]}
